{"name":"Grounding / earthing mat","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Westjet_planes_grounding_at_Yeg_airport_during_Covid-19_impact.jpg/960px-Westjet_planes_grounding_at_Yeg_airport_during_Covid-19_impact.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Westjet_planes_grounding_at_Yeg_airport_during_Covid-19_impact.jpg","caption":"Westjet planes grounding at Yeg airport during Covid-19 impact","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":2,"casual":{"lead":["Grounding or earthing products are conductive mats, sheets or bands that plug into a wall socket's ground port or a ground rod. People sleep on them hoping for deeper sleep and less inflammation, which they connect to a fresher, more rested appearance.","Proponents say electrons from the earth's surface neutralise free radicals in the body. Encyclopedic sources list earthing as an alternative medicine practice, and no clinical trials were retrieved for sleep or appearance outcomes."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Users lay the mat on the bed or desk, or wear a band, and connect it to the ground port of a wall outlet or to a ground rod. It is typically used nightly as part of a sleep setup. Users describe judging the effect over weeks of sleep quality."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["The product is a passive conductive fabric, but connecting through a wall outlet raises electrical-safety questions that manufacturers address with built-in resistors. The sources reviewed provide no safety data. Checking that the outlet is properly grounded is a commonly stated precaution."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Westjet_planes_grounding_at_Yeg_airport_during_Covid-19_impact.jpg/960px-Westjet_planes_grounding_at_Yeg_airport_during_Covid-19_impact.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imagein